{"name":"Light Dante Peak","hex":"#c6dedf","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"light","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Electromagnetic radiation in the wavelength range visible to the human eye (about 400–750 nanometers): visible light.","Electromagnetic radiation in the wavelength range visible to the human eye or in nearby ranges (infrared or ultraviolet radiation)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To start (a fire).","To set fire to; to set burning."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/light"},{"term":"peak","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A point; the sharp end or top of anything that terminates in a point; as, the peak, or front, of a cap.","The highest value reached by some quantity in a time period."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To raise the point of (a gaff) closer to perpendicular.","To raise an oar out of the water, fitting the handle into a round slot or socket located at the bottom of the boat."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/peak"}],"entries":[{"title":"Dante Alighieri","blocks":[{"text":"Dante Alighieri, widely known mononymously as Dante, was an Italian poet, writer, and philosopher. His Divine Comedy, originally called Comedìa and later christened Divina by Giovanni Boccaccio, is widely considered one of the most important poems of the Middle Ages and the greatest literary work in the Italian language."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Bargello_-_Kapelle_Fresko_2a.jpg/330px-Bargello_-_Kapelle_Fresko_2a.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dante_Alighieri","wikidata":"Q1067"},{"title":"Light","blocks":[{"text":"Light, visible light, or visible radiation is electromagnetic radiation that can be perceived by the human eye. Visible light spans the visible spectrum and is usually defined as having wavelengths in the range of 400–700 nanometers (nm), corresponding t